  data: {
    LLM: "Score the most points in the deal (card points, Cantes, last trick). Follow suit and overtake when possible; trump if void. Declare 40 or 20 after winning a trick; Tute (4 Kings or 4 Knights) wins the deal outright.\n\nDealer deals 10 cards each; next card is trump, rest form stock. Player to dealer's right leads. Follow suit; must beat led suit if possible; if void must trump if possible. Trick winner draws first from stock, then opponent. After winning a trick you may declare one Cante (King+Horse of same suit: 40 in trumps, 20 in other). Declaring Tute (all four Kings or all four Horses) wins the deal. Last trick scores 10 extra. Most points wins the deal.",
    Player: "Score the most points in the deal (card points, Cantes, last trick). Follow suit and overtake when possible; trump if void. Declare 40 or 20 after winning a trick; Tute (4 Kings or 4 Knights) wins the deal outright.\n\nDealer deals 10 cards each; next card is trump, rest form stock. Player to dealer's right leads. Follow suit; must beat led suit if possible; if void must trump if possible. Trick winner draws first from stock, then opponent. After winning a trick you may declare one Cante (King+Horse of same suit: 40 in trumps, 20 in other). Declaring Tute (all four Kings or all four Horses) wins the deal. Last trick scores 10 extra. Most points wins the deal.",
